<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  THE SEAMLESS SUB-PAGE TOOLBAR (owner request 0.4.6).
  00-rules.md 4.8, 22-components.md 12.1, 32-master-plan-android.md 8.6.
  ============================================================================

  The header is not a bar, it is the top of the page. Same background as the page,
  no elevation, no divider, no shadow, no scrim, no AppBarLayout tint, no
  liftOnScroll. This one file is the fix for every peripheral screen at once — the
  most repeated defect in the app is a sub-page whose Russian title is drawn in the
  20sp Latin wordmark face, which has no Cyrillic at all (D-11).

      [ 12 ][ back, 24 glyph ][ 16 ][ Title 16/700 ][ flex ][ action (0-1) ][ 14 ]

  THE GUTTER ARITHMETIC, because it is the part that gets rebuilt wrong — and it was,
  three times. Both controls are an EXACT 48dp box (14.2) holding a 24dp glyph, and what
  places that glyph is neither a padding nor a margin: MaterialButton's iconGravity is
  textStart, so the library CENTRES the icon and then shifts it by half the difference
  between the two paddings. With a symmetric padding — which is now the style's, for both
  slots — the glyph sits at the box's centre and the press plate, which is the box less
  its insets, sits concentric with it. The insets are then split per slot to carry glyph
  and plate together to the gutter each one has to reach.

  THE BOXES USED TO BE wrap_content, and that is what made every number in this file
  fiction: a MaterialButton with no text still measures a line box, so the back control
  was laid out 68 × 64 and the action 80 × 64, the «28dp disc» was a 48×44 and a 54×44
  stadium, and the title started at 72 rather than the 52 below. An icon-only control has
  no text to grow with the font scale, so an exact 48 costs nothing here.

  Owner report 0.4.9, «эту кнопку нужно сделать чуть левее»: the control now sits FLUSH
  with the screen edge and its glyph at 12, four dp left of §7's nominal 16. §7's
  «−10dp влево» exists so the GLYPH lands on the gutter rather than the edge of its
  touch target; the owner asked for a touch more, and the target reaching the screen
  edge is a Fitts's-law gain rather than a cost. The invariant that matters downstream
  still holds: the glyph ends at 36 and the title's marginStart space_4 lands it at 52,
  16 clear of the glyph, exactly as before.

  THE TRAILING ACTION IS ON THE GUTTER NOW, and its box no longer leaves the screen to
  get there. @dimen/toolbar_plate_inset_lead splits the slot's 20dp of inset 16/4, which
  moves glyph and plate 6dp toward the trailing edge inside a box that stays 48 wide;
  ToolbarBinder then holds the box off the edge by whatever the glyph's own air leaves
  (0 for «⋮», 5 for «+»). Both inks end on 16 — where the title starts, where every row's
  trailing glyph stops, the one gutter CLAUDE.md gives the product — with all 48dp of the
  target on screen and the press disc 4dp clear of the window. «вот нашел что плюсик
  сверху он левее, надо правее опять сделать».

  THE BACK ARROW STAYS AT 20 and that is a decision, not an oversight. Its ink is 20
  from the leading edge against the action's 16 on the other side, so the header is 4dp
  asymmetric — read the note on @id/toolbar_back for why 20 is the number that keeps
  its 48dp target whole and why the text under it is not the thing it should be
  levelled with.

  56 IS A MINIMUM, NEVER A HEIGHT. At font scale 200% a 16sp title needs ~34dp of
  line box and this bar grows to hold it. android:layout_height="56dp" on anything
  containing text is a P1 accessibility defect (14.5).

  ON A TAB SCREEN there is no back affordance and the title starts at the gutter:
      toolbarBack.isVisible = false
      toolbarLeadingGap.isVisible = true      <- 12 + the title's 4 = the 16 gutter
  Home is the ONE screen that keeps the wordmark: it applies
  @style/ToolbarBrandTitle to @id/toolbar_title and nothing else in the app may.

  THE HAIRLINE IS THE ONLY PERMITTED BOUNDARY and it ships at alpha 0. If a screen
  genuinely needs a boundary once its content is scrolled, it fades the hairline in
  over motion_state 220ms at scrollY > 0 and back out at the top. It never appears
  at rest, and nothing else about this bar changes on scroll — no colour, no
  elevation, no shadow.
-->
<LinearLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    android:id="@+id/toolbar"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
    android:background="?android:attr/colorBackground"
    android:elevation="0dp"
    android:orientation="vertical">

    <LinearLayout
        android:id="@+id/toolbar_bar"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:baselineAligned="false"
        android:gravity="center_vertical"
        android:minHeight="@dimen/toolbar_height"
        android:orientation="horizontal">

        <!-- ICON GAP CLOSED: @drawable/ic_chevron_left is a real left-pointing glyph now.
             It used to be ic_chevron_right under android:scaleX="-1", and that mirror
             never reached the screen — @anim/press_icon, which this style carries, has a
             DEFAULT item that animates scaleX to 1.0 and it fires on attach, so the
             arrow shipped pointing right. Do not reintroduce a scaleX mirror here; the
             new drawable is android:autoMirrored, which is what RTL needs anyway.
             STRING GAP CLOSED (M-44): this was the tree's one hardcoded
             android:contentDescription. It is now @string/cd_back, defined in
             res/values/strings_ui_polish.xml — the toolbar belongs to no single screen,
             so its one string lives in the cross-cutting file rather than a screen's.

             WHY ITS INK STAYS AT 20 WHILE THE ACTION MOVED TO 16. The two are not the
             same problem read in a mirror:

             1. The box is FLUSH with the screen edge (owner report 0.4.9, «эту кнопку
                нужно сделать чуть левее»), so all 48dp of the target is on screen and
                the leading edge of the screen is part of it — a Fitts's-law gain the
                trailing action cannot have. Moving the ink to 16 needs the box at −4,
                which leaves 44dp touchable: a 14.2 regression on the one control every
                sub-page must always answer, bought for 4dp.
             2. What it would be levelling with is TEXT, and a text box on the 16dp
                gutter starts its INK a dp or two inside it. The arrow at 20 is ~2.5dp
                off the title's first stroke, not 4, and at 16 it would overshoot to the
                left of it. The trailing slot has no such slack: it is compared with the
                card edges and the row glyphs directly under it, which stop on 16 exactly.

             So the header is 4dp asymmetric on purpose. If the owner asks for this
             arrow again, the move is layout_marginStart −4 here and in
             view_sub_header.xml, plus expandTouchTarget(56) in ToolbarBinder to give
             back the 4dp of target — not a change to any number in dimens.xml.

             WHAT DID CHANGE FOR IT is the box and the press plate. The box is an EXACT
             48 now instead of wrap_content: a MaterialButton with no text still measures
             a line box, so this control was laid out 68 wide and 64 tall, its «28dp disc»
             was really a 48×44 stadium, and the title beside it started at 72 rather than
             the 52 this file promises. An icon-only control has nothing to grow, so an
             exact 48 is free and every number here becomes deterministic.

             ITS PADDING IS THE STYLE'S NOW. The 12 written here was doing nothing the
             comment above claimed: iconGravity is textStart, so the glyph is CENTRED by
             the library and only the difference between the two paddings moves it. Equal
             is all that is required, and equal is what keeps the press disc concentric
             with the glyph. -->
        <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
            android:id="@+id/toolbar_back"
            style="@style/Widget.Departament.Button.Icon.Toolbar"
            android:layout_width="@dimen/view_height_dp48"
            android:layout_height="@dimen/view_height_dp48"
            android:contentDescription="@string/cd_back"
            app:icon="@drawable/ic_chevron_left" />

        <!-- Shown ONLY when the back control is hidden, so a tab screen's title still
             starts at the 16dp gutter (12 here + the title's 4). -->
        <Space
            android:id="@+id/toolbar_leading_gap"
            android:layout_width="@dimen/space_12"
            android:layout_height="0dp"
            android:visibility="gone" />

        <TextView
            android:id="@+id/toolbar_title"
            android:layout_width="0dp"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/space_4"
            android:layout_marginEnd="@dimen/space_12"
            android:layout_weight="1"
            android:ellipsize="end"
            android:maxLines="1"
            android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Title"
            tools:text="Маршрутизация" />

        <!-- AT MOST ONE. A second action becomes an overflow whose glyph is
             ic_more_vert_24dp. The caller sets app:icon AND
             android:contentDescription, which states the action and not the object.

             WHAT MOVES ITS GLYPH IS THE INSET SPLIT, NOT A PADDING PAIR, and that is the
             correction this round makes. The 18/12 padding written here was measured for
             a glyph parked at paddingLeft; iconGravity is textStart, so the glyph is
             centred and an asymmetric padding only shifts it by half the difference —
             3dp off the press disc it sits on, «фон не по центру, неровный фон». The
             padding is symmetric (the style's) and the 20dp of inset is split 16/4
             instead: box and disc both stay 48 and 28, and the pair carries glyph AND
             plate 6dp toward the trailing edge together. See
             @dimen/toolbar_plate_inset_lead.

             AND NO 4dp MARGIN. It had one, and ToolbarBinder overwrites marginEnd on
             every bind, so the 4 only ever applied to a glyph the binder does not know.
             The binder's own margin is non-negative now, so the whole 48dp box is on
             screen for both glyphs. -->
        <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
            android:id="@+id/toolbar_action"
            style="@style/Widget.Departament.Button.Icon.Toolbar"
            android:layout_width="@dimen/view_height_dp48"
            android:layout_height="@dimen/view_height_dp48"
            android:insetLeft="@dimen/toolbar_plate_inset_lead"
            android:insetRight="@dimen/toolbar_plate_inset_trail"
            android:visibility="gone"
            app:icon="@drawable/ic_more_vert_24dp"
            tools:ignore="ContentDescription"
            tools:visibility="visible" />
    </LinearLayout>

    <View
        android:id="@+id/toolbar_hairline"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="@dimen/stroke_hairline"
        android:alpha="0"
        android:background="?attr/colorOutlineVariant" />
</LinearLayout>
